// Nekoro Random Drop: extra drops from blocks, mobs and (with Cobblemon) Pokemon.
// Every rule is rolled on its own. After editing, use /randomdrop reload in game (/reload works too).
//
// "source"       "block", "mob", "pokemon_kill" (killed or defeated in battle) or "pokemon_catch"
// "match"        block or entity id, or a tag starting with #. A list works too: ["minecraft:stone", "#c:ores"]
//                Pokemon rules: species ids, optional (for example "cobblemon:pikachu")
// "type"         Pokemon rules only, optional: "fire" or ["fire", "water"]
// "item"         item to give (can be left out if the rule only gives xp)
// "count"        how many items, default 1
// "chance"       0.0 to 1.0, default 1.0 (always). 0.005 is 0.5%
// "xp"           experience points, default 0
// "bonus"        how Fortune (blocks) or Looting (mobs) helps, default "multiply":
//                "multiply" like vanilla ores, works with any enchantment level
//                "chance"   chance x (level + 1)
//                "none"
// "silk_touch"   blocks only, what happens when the block is mined with Silk Touch, default false:
//                false    no drop
//                true     drops as usual
//                "bonus"  the chance goes up with the Silk Touch level, see silk_touch_bonus_per_level below
// "player_only"  only when a player mines the block or kills the mob, default true
// "to_inventory" put the reward straight into the player's inventory, default false (dropped on the ground);
//                xp then appears at the player instead, so Mending still gets it
// "cooldown"     ticks before the same player can get this rule again, default 0 (20 ticks = 1 second)
// "min_tool"     the tool (blocks) or weapon (mobs) must be at least this tier: "wood", "stone", "iron",
//                "diamond" or "netherite". E.g. "iron" for diamonds, like mining a diamond ore
//
// Where it works (all optional, checked at the mined block, the dead mob or the player who caught the Pokemon):
// "min_y"        lowest Y level, included. "max_y": highest Y level, included
// "dimension"    dimension id or a list: "minecraft:overworld", "minecraft:the_nether", "minecraft:the_end"
// "biome"        biome id or a biome tag starting with #, a list works too: ["minecraft:lush_caves", "#c:is_ocean"]
{
  // For "silk_touch": "bonus" rules: Silk Touch I keeps the normal chance and every level above adds this much.
  // 1.0: II doubles the chance, X makes it 10 times higher. 0.5: II 1.5 times, X 5.5 times. 0: no bonus.
  // Levels above I need a mod that raises enchantment levels, for example Nekoro World Setup.
  "silk_touch_bonus_per_level": 1.0,

  "rules": [
    // ORES FROM STONE
    // The rules below make mined stone and deepslate drop ores about as often as vanilla ore generation
    // would give them at that height, so they are meant for worlds WITHOUT ores (for example with
    // "remove_ores" in Nekoro World Setup). If your world still generates ores, delete these rules,
    // or you get ores twice. Deepslate drops twice as often, because it takes longer to mine.
    // Below Y 0 every kind drops; emeralds are 10 times more common in mountains, gold in badlands.
    // ores: worked out from vanilla ore placement
